  - 3\: AA, Aa, aa
  - 2\: BB, Bb
  - 2\: Cc, cc
  - 1\: Dd
  - 3\: EE, Ee, ee
- 3 × 2 × 2 × 1 × 3 = [36 genotypes]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# Genotypes in F2 hybrid crosses

@body

- Only works with heterozygotes for all genes!
- you use 3\^n to find the number of genotype and 2\^n to find the number of phenotypes
- monohybrid
  - 3\^1 = 3
  - AA, Aa, aa
- dihybrid
  - 3\^2 = 9
  - AABB, AABb, AAbb, AaBB, AaBb, Aabb, aaBB, aaBb, aabb
- trihybrid
  - 3\^3 = 27
  - all the dihybrids times three with CC, Cc, cc swapped
- tetrahybrid
  - 3\^4 = 81
  - DD, Dd, dd, etc.

