- test-cross\:
  - aa bb cc dd ee × AA Bb Cc DD Ee
- Step 2\: what are the possible genotypes for each gene separately?
  - 1\: all Aa
  - 2\: Bb or bb
  - 2\: Cc or cc
  - 1\: all Dd
  - 2\: Ee or ee

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 5](assets/lect04h-indep_assort_problems/image_005.png)

- Step 2\: what are the gametes?
  - 1\: Aa – 2\: Bb, bb – 2\: Cc, cc – 1\: Dd – 2\: Ee, ee
- Step 3\: What are heterozygote probabilities of each gene’s genotype?
  - Aa\: 100%
  - Bb\: 50%
  - Cc\: 50%
  - Dd\: 100%
  - Ee\: 50%

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 5](assets/lect04h-indep_assort_problems/image_005.png)

- Step 3\: What are probabilities of each gene’s genotype?
  - Aa\: 100%
  - Bb\: 50%
  - Cc\: 50%
  - Dd\: 100%
  - Ee\: 50%
- Step 4\: Are they independent?

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 5](assets/lect04h-indep_assort_problems/image_005.png)

- Step 3\: What are probabilities of each gene’s genotype?
  - Aa\: 100% -- Bb\: 50% -- Cc\: 50% -- Dd\: 100% -- Ee\: 50%
- Step 4\: Are they independent?
  - Yes, states independent assortment above
- Multiplication rule\:
- 1 × ½ × ½ × 1 × ½ = [1/8]{color=red}

=== layout: section

# A Problem of Seven Genes

=== layout: one-panel

# Seven Gene Gamete Formation

@body

- How many possible gametes?
- Look if there is only one allele
- AA bb Cc DD Ee FF gg

=== layout: one-panel

# Seven Gene Gamete Formation

@body

- Genotype of all unlinked genes\:
- Look if there is only one allele
- AA    bb   Cc    DD    Ee   FF   gg
- A     b             D            F    g
- C or c            E or e

=== layout: one-panel

# Seven Gene Gamete Formation

@body

- Genotype of all unlinked genes\:
- Look if there is only one allele
- AA bb Cc DD Ee FF gg
  - 1 × 1 × 2 × 1 × 2 × 1 × 1 = 4
- Only Four Possible Gametes\:
  - AbCDEFg
  - AbCDeFg
  - AbcDEFg
  - AbcDeFg

